Z||000000||Captain Kirk*||11-27-2001||09:30 PM||||I have a 88 fiero GT and it has 105K miles on it and I was thinking of buying the Kit from the FIero Store but I want to know what kinda goodys it will bring my car.<P>Will it make the engine last longer?<BR>Or is almost like buying a new engine?||||reg||5
Z||000001||avengador1||11-27-2001||09:35 PM||||Make sure you get the right size pistons if you plan to have the engine bored out. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Captain Kirk*||11-27-2001||09:51 PM||||Another question:How much does it cost to get someone to install it?||||reg||5
Z||000003||FieroPerformance||11-27-2001||09:55 PM||||The Fiero Store's kit is a bit high priced. I'd check around, most machine shops will be able to get the parts for cheaper. I just got done rebuilding my engine. I had the block, heads, crank and connecting rods reconditioned. I put in a powermax 2030 performance cam shaft, and high compression power forged pistons. I replaced just about everything else in the engine with stock spec parts. I also put in a heavy duty clutch and pressure plate. All together I spent about $2,000 (including the $750 in machine work). It feels like a new engine and is much faster. I have 160 miles on it now. The kit from the Fiero Store does not include all of the things that I put in.<P>Just my .02, I hope it helps a little bit.<P>-Charlie<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsigfperformance.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||ThatRickGuy||11-27-2001||11:16 PM||||I did a 3.2 rebuild last year, all in all was arroun $2400 when the car got back on the road, but that was with all internal goodies, east coast price machine work and assembly, and new battery, altinator, and starter along with some other odds and ends that needed replacing. to tell the truth, to do it over again, I'd probrably pick up a crate 3.4 from gm performance parts, they go for $1600-1800, you still have to get the starter remounted, but you can probrably find a machine shop to take car of that for not much.||||reg||1
